WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.056
Controllers translate HTTP requests into application operations and translate results back into

00:00:06.056 --> 00:00:07.570
the API contract.

00:00:07.720 --> 00:00:12.993
Keep business rules in services, persistence in repositories, and request validation at

00:00:12.993 --> 00:00:13.872
the boundary.

00:00:14.022 --> 00:00:19.052
DTOs prevent persistence details from accidentally becoming public JSON fields.

00:00:19.202 --> 00:00:23.717
They also avoid serializing lazy relationships or recursive entity graphs.

00:00:23.867 --> 00:00:26.027
Pagination must be bounded and ordered.

00:00:26.177 --> 00:00:29.871
A page without a stable sort can repeat or omit records as

00:00:29.871 --> 00:00:30.795
the database changes.

00:00:30.945 --> 00:00:35.962
Offset pagination is simple for small datasets; keyset pagination can work better

00:00:35.962 --> 00:00:37.635
for deep sequential browsing.

00:00:37.785 --> 00:00:42.158
Define maximum page size so one request cannot fetch the entire table.

00:00:42.308 --> 00:00:47.136
InventoryController maps products to ProductView records and accepts page sizes from one

00:00:47.136 --> 00:00:48.343
to one hundred.

00:00:48.493 --> 00:00:50.208
It sorts by product ID.

00:00:50.358 --> 00:00:55.272
OrderController exposes only ID, product, quantity, and status.

00:00:55.422 --> 00:01:00.370
Internal idempotency keys and JPA version fields are not automatically serialized from

00:01:00.370 --> 00:01:01.608
the order entity.

00:01:01.758 --> 00:01:05.238
Add GET /products/{id} and a product search endpoint.

00:01:05.388 --> 00:01:11.089
Return explicit DTOs, validate pagination limits, and test the empty page and

00:01:11.089 --> 00:01:13.464
unknown product cases over HTTP.

00:01:13.614 --> 00:01:17.229
Map an unknown product to the documented 404 response.

00:01:17.379 --> 00:01:21.000
Keep search inputs parameterized through repository APIs.

00:01:21.150 --> 00:01:25.047
Use a deterministic sort with a tie-breaker and state whether the endpoint

00:01:25.047 --> 00:01:27.970
returns a total count or only a next-page indicator.

00:01:28.120 --> 00:01:28.791
Question.

00:01:28.941 --> 00:01:32.252
Why avoid returning JPA entities from controllers?

00:01:32.402 --> 00:01:32.979
Answer.

00:01:33.129 --> 00:01:37.585
It couples the public API to persistence structure and can expose internal

00:01:37.585 --> 00:01:39.813
fields or trigger unexpected lazy loads.

00:01:39.963 --> 00:01:40.634
Question.

00:01:40.784 --> 00:01:42.482
What is keyset pagination?

00:01:42.632 --> 00:01:43.209
Answer.

00:01:43.359 --> 00:01:47.547
Fetching rows after a stable ordered cursor, such as a last-seen ID,

00:01:47.547 --> 00:01:49.642
instead of skipping a growing offset.
